criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* women and individuals assigned female at birth (AFAB) aged 40-65 years of age;
* subjective distressing vasomotor symptoms (a score of 30 or higher on the Hot Flash Rating Scale);
* residing in Canada;
* fluent in English;
* access to, and comfort with, the internet and a computer;
* not currently engaged in psychotherapy;
* not taking hormonal or psychotropic medication or if taking medication, stable in type and dose for 8 weeks prior to study and stable for duration of the study

Exclusion Criteria:

* participants with severe depression (as a score of 15 and over on the PHQ-9 or active suicidal ideation or psychotic symptoms;
* participants with a severe mental health disorder requiring in-person therapy (e.g., severe substance abuse, recent history of psychosis or mania);
* participants with an unstable general medical condition;
* participants with cognitive impairment that would limit comprehension or ability to engage with the online program.
